Contrib: hg_alarm

After installation of this contrib, you will get 4 files:
    1. hg_alarm: 
        An executable file under '$INSTALL/bin'.
    2. hg_alarm.so: 
        A dynamic loadable library under '$INSTALL/lib/postgresql'.
    3. hg_alarm--1.0.sql
        A SQL script under '$INSTALL/share/postgresql/extension'.
    4. hg_alarm_conf.example:
        A template configuration file under '$INSTALL/share/doc/contrib'.

hg_alarm:
    Usage:
        ./hg_alarm OPERATION [-c] config-file-path [Options...]

    While OPERATION can be 'start' or 'stop', the 'stop' opeartion aoto-
    ignore any options provide, For 'start' operation:

    The config-file-path must be provided in json format. A template is 
    provided ($INSTALL/share/doc/contrib/hg_alarm_conf.example), users 
    may use it to customize their own configuration.

    hg_alarm is a simple daemon process to check config-threshold(s) 
    registered in the conf file cyclically.

    All options of 'hg_alarm' can alse be set in the config file, but the
    options provided by cmd will overwrite them.

    Try hg_alarm --help/-? for more details.

hg_alarm.so:
hg_alarm--1.0.sql:
    These two files are used to create the hg_alarm extension.

    The 'hg_alarm.so' defines the C language functions impl(s) of the SQL 
    functions defined in 'hg_alarm--1.0.sql'.

    Two SQL functions will be created after 'CREATE EXTENSION hg_alarm'.

    1. hg_alarm_check(cfgpath, cfgname)
        The backend who calls this routine simply parses the conf file to
        get the threshold of the config specified by 'cfgname', and check
        if current config value is out of it.

        Returns 'True' if the config is still under control or 'False' if 
        it is out of limitation.

    2. hg_alarm_stat(cfgpath)
        The backend who calls this routine simply parses the conf file to
        get all configs and current config values.

        Returns a table of tuples in a format: (cfgname, cfgcur, cfglimit)
        
hg_alarm_conf.example:
    A template configuration file.